A||||0||PaUL||Fiero Next of Kin
Z||000000||PaUL||04-19-99||06:01 PM||||Hi,<br>Ive been thinking about the Fiero and other cars that are related. We all know that Fiero is the antithesis of corp parts bin engineering and is directly related to other models like the chevette and citation, but did you know that it has some even more distant relatives? The chevette was originally designed by Isuzu, being based on an old Aska platform. The first generation Impulse is based on the chevette, so that makes it a distant cousin. The engines for the second gen Impulse and Geo Storm have the same trans bolt pattern and you could drop an Isuzu motor into a fiero, although I dont see why. The shortlived Lotus Elan also used an Isuzu engine. By the way Kia of Korea has bought the rights to the Elan and is producing it in Korea. <p>Just some interesting tidbits. <br>
